ed_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"wF-L8lZGy2H1q_06KJUHwg","review_id":"LNHRMglCF_R8cxsCqz12QA","date":"2012-08-09T14:18:30","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9147967100143433,"text_excerpt":"I've been to Ralph and Kacoo's twice now and have been thrilled both times. The service and the food is incredible. The first time I visited Ralph and Kacoo's I was with a couple of friends and we wanted an afternoon snack. This place was suggested to us and we shared the \"Taste of Louisiana\" (trio of fried crawfish tails, alligator and popcorn shrimp). It was my first time to ever try crawfish or alligator and it made me an instant fan of both. The second time I visited there were about 7 or 8 of us for dinner. For the life of me (what does that mean?) I cannot remember what I ordered, but I remember that it was absolutely delicious. We were a rather rowdy, loud group, but we were treate..."},{"business_id":"wF-L8lZGy2H1q_06KJUHwg","review_id":"Zn50_kqCimhDuI91BqDh9A","date":"2008-04-25T19:24:52","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9147957563400269,"text_excerpt":"The service is worth the visit. I've only been once, but the server was worth the cost of the meal. I had the \"whale\" sized fried soft shell crab and it was the biggest soft shell crab I've ever seen. It was good. The gumbo was way way above average but it did have a few shell pieces in it. This place is one that you should give a try if you'll be in New Orleans a few nights. Nice, quiet, cozy place with GREAT service and really good food."},{"business_id":"wF-L8lZGy2H1q_06KJUHwg","review_id":"BbyewxDmx8jQNCeYfvv2bQ","date":"2013-08-30T11:51:52","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9144964218139648,"text_excerpt":"Food is great. Drinks are delicious. Great location & atmosphere. The service was pretty good too. We started off with some raw oysters they were ok. I had the stuffed fish topped with shrimp and sauce (really good) with side of asparagus (just ok)."}],"visual":